    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d285">

                <pb facs="0727" n="699" sameAs="frus:frus1945-50Intel/pg699"/>

                <head>285. Memorandum From the Assistant Executive Secretary of the National
                    Security Council (Lay) to
                    Director of Central Intelligence Hillenkoetter<anchor n="0" xml:id="d285-f1"/></head>
                <dateline><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1948-06-07">June 7, 1948</date>.</dateline>
                <p>Attached is the proposed NSC Directive which is
                    based upon your paper of June 4, 1948 on the establishment of an Office of
                    Special Services.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d285-f2"/></p>
                <pb facs="0728" n="700" xml:id="pg700"/>
                <p>As indicated in our phone conversation this morning, the attached will be
                    discussed at an NSC Staff meeting at 10:00 a.m.
                    tomorrow in Room 224, Old State Building.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#bold">James S. Lay, Jr.</hi>
                        <anchor n="2" xml:id="d285-f3"/>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d285-a1.xml" xpointer="d285-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
